# CODEOWNERS
#
# Scope: ONLY hardfork-frozen precompile logic and versions.rs, which pins
# each frozen file's hash at compile time (see versions.rs) - not the
# precompiles crate as a whole, and not dispatch/precompile entrypoints
# (those change routinely as versions/precompiles are added and carry no
# freeze guarantee).
#
# This is a review-gate and audit trail, not cryptographic immutability: a PR
# that edits a frozen file can also edit the pinned hash in versions.rs in the
# same commit - the compile-time assert only proves the two are consistent
# with each other, not that the pinned hash is the "right" one. The real
# control is "a named owner below must approve."
#
# Trade-off, by design: gating versions.rs means every new hardfork's version
# addition (routine, frequent) requires the same sign-off as tampering with an
# existing frozen arm or its pinned hash (rare, dangerous) - accepted because
# versions.rs is the single source of truth for both, and path-based
# CODEOWNERS can't distinguish the two.
#
# Forward-looking: `*` matches one path segment, so this also covers any
# future precompile solidified via /solidify-precompile (e.g. b20_asset,
# b20_factory) once it gains its own logic/ + versions.rs, with no further
# edits needed here.
#
# ACTION REQUIRED (not delivered by this file): a repo admin must enable
# "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection settings for main.
# Until that toggle is flipped, this file is purely advisory - GitHub will
# not block merges on it. No Terraform/IaC manages branch protection in this
# repo today, so this cannot be done as a code change.

